38:  * Different constructor variants allow you to configure {@code dataSourceClassName} (note that HikariCP uses {@code javax.sql.DataSource} instances
39:  * instead of {@code java.sql.Driver} used by other connection pools), {@code minimumPoolSize} and {@code maximumPoolSize} as well as {@code dataSourceProperties}.
40:  * </p>
41:  * <p>
42:  * If you wish to configure the module using configuration properties you should use the following property names: {@code other.hikari.dataSourceClassName},
43:  * {@code other.hikari.minimumPoolSize} and {@code other.hikari.maximumPoolSize}. All configuration properties prefixed with {@code other.hikari.dataSourceProperties} will
44:  * be used as data source properties - e.g. {@code other.hikari.URL} will be used to set {@code URL} property on the data source.
45:  * </p>
46:  * <p>
