272:    * <p>
273:    * The returned Maybe emits the promise's single value if it succeeds, and emits the error (i.e. via {@code onError()}) if it fails.
274:    * <p>
275:    * This method works well as a method reference to the {@link Promise#to(ratpack.func.Function)} method.
276:    * <pre class="java">{@code
277:    * import ratpack.rx2.RxRatpack;
278:    * import ratpack.exec.Promise;
279:    * import ratpack.test.exec.ExecHarness;
280:    *
281:    * import static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;
282:    *
283:    * public class Example {
284:    *   public static String value;
285:    *   public static void main(String... args) throws Exception {
286:    *     ExecHarness.runSingle(e ->
287:    *       Promise.value("hello world")
288:    *       .to(RxRatpack::maybe)
289:    *       .map(String::toUpperCase)
290:    *       .subscribe(s -> value = s)
291:    *     );
292:    *
293:    *     assertEquals("HELLO WORLD", value);
294:    *   }
295:    * }
296:    * }</pre>
297:    *
298:    * @param promise the promise
299:    * @param <T>     the type of value promised
300:    * @return a maybe for the promised value
301:    */
302:   public static <T> Maybe<T> maybe(Promise<T> promise) {
303:     return Maybe.create(subscriber ->
304:       promise.onError(subscriber::onError).then(value -> {
305:         subscriber.onSuccess(value);
306:         subscriber.onComplete();
307:       })
308:     );
309:   }
